-- #1111 A-2.3 BYSTANDER FIXTURE — "feature + UNRELATED code still behaves",
-- which is the shape `AGENTS.md` requires of any change that re-keys a
-- PROGRAM-GLOBAL TABLE, as opposed to "feature works".
--
-- A-2.3 re-keys `aliasTableRef` / `dataParamKindsRef` (`compiler/types/
-- typecheck.mdk`) from a bare type name to a module-qualified identity.  The
-- fixtures that prove the FEATURE are the drained #1069/#1090/#1070 repros —
-- each one asserts that a SHADOWED name now resolves to the right module.  This
-- fixture asserts the other half, which no drained repro can: that a module
-- which shadows NOTHING is inferred exactly as it would be with no collision in
-- the graph at all.
--
-- The graph DOES contain a collision: `dupa.mdk` and `dupz.mdk` both declare a
-- type `Dup` at arity 2 (one with a row-kinded slot 0, one all-Type) and an
-- alias `Shared` (Int vs Float).  Only their unrelated FUNCTIONS are imported,
-- so both are registered into the cross-module universe and neither is nameable
-- from here.  NOTHING BELOW MENTIONS `Dup` OR `Shared`.
--
-- What the golden pins, and why each line can fail:
--   * `w` writes a BARE row into `Widget`'s KRow slot.  A lookup that missed
--     would fall to `appFallback`, the row would land in an ordinary type slot,
--     and `fromAstTypeE`'s `TyRow` arm would raise T-EFFECT-KIND-MISMATCH — the
--     binding would vanish from the dump (#1090's symptom, on a name that
--     collides with nothing).
--   * `wrapped` writes the WRAPPED spelling of the same row.  A miss there is
--     SILENT: `fromAstTypeE`'s `TyEffect` arm unwraps to the real type and
--     inference continues, so the scheme would read `Widget Unit Int` (#1069's
--     symptom).  Both spellings are pinned because the two failure modes are
--     different and each is invisible to the other.
--   * `g` / `p` exercise the alias table's alias-of-alias and saturated
--     parameterized arms; a wrong expansion shows as a different scheme
--     (#1070's symptom).
--   * `lst` / `opt` / `n` mention NONE of A-2.3's machinery — builtin and
--     prelude heads, which have no row in either table and reach the
--     `appFallback` miss path deliberately (miss-policy case 1).  They are here
--     to answer `AGENTS.md`'s "what happens to a program that never touches the
--     table" directly.
import plain.{Widget, Pair, MkPair, Gauge2, Boxed}
import dupa.{da} -- ONLY the function; never dupa's Dup or Shared
import dupz.{dz} -- ONLY the function; never dupz's Dup or Shared

w : Widget <Stdout> Int
w = w

wrapped : Widget (<Stdout> Unit) Int
wrapped = wrapped

g : Gauge2
g = 7

p : Boxed Int
p = MkPair 1 2

lst : List Int
lst = [1, 2, 3]

opt : Option String
opt = Some "s"

n : Int
n = da (dz 1)
